# encoder: the DB8E screen is select-gated like the ring and the button.
# Spec: hardware.md §6.12 "Circuits with user interaction" — the screen shows the
# state of the circuit you are actually operating; encoder.md's select/selectat
# route a shared knob to the currently selected overlay circuit, and the ring
# already follows that (issue #15). The screen must follow it too: a DESELECTED
# overlay circuit never writes, even when its value keeps moving underneath.
#
# Two circuits share E1.1. A (selectat 0) is selected throughout; B (selectat 1)
# never is, but its value is driven by `override`, so it changes without anyone
# touching the knob — encoder.md: "override honors select, so if you use select,
# it does nothing ... while the encoder circuit is not selected".
# Scales are kept small so the `output` jacks stay inside the +-10 V (+-1.0)
# clamp and it is the display, not the clamp, that is under test.
#   t1: turn +48 -> A consumes it (pos 0.5) -> A shows 0.5*0.1 + 0.1 = 0.15
#   t2: override drives B to 1.0 -> B's own output becomes 1.0, but B is
#       deselected -> no write; the screen still reads A's 0.15
#   t3: override drives B to 0.2 -> B's output 0.92 -> still no write
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[db8e]

[encoder]
    encoder      = E1.1
    smooth       = 0
    select       = I2
    selectat     = 0
    outputscale  = 0.1
    outputoffset = 0.1
    output       = O1

[encoder]
    encoder      = E1.1
    smooth       = 0
    select       = I2
    selectat     = 1
    override     = I3
    outputscale  = 0.1
    outputoffset = 0.9
    output       = O2
>>>
@0 expectdisplay D1 off
@1 turn E1.1 48
@1 expectdisplay D1 value 0.15 tol 1e-6
@2 set I3 1
@2 expect O2 1.0 tol 1e-6
@2 expectdisplay D1 value 0.15 tol 1e-6
@3 set I3 0.2
@3 expect O2 0.92 tol 1e-6
@3 expectdisplay D1 value 0.15 tol 1e-6
